import Spaces.Supported.StandardTStructure
import Spaces.Supported.NeemanAbstract

/-!
# The standard `t`-structure of `D_{qc,Z}(X)` and the preferred equivalence class

GL26 **Lemma A.9** (`lem:preferred_eq_class`), preferred-class clause: for a quasi-compact
quasi-separated algebraic space `X` and a closed `Z ⊆ |X|` with quasi-compact complement, the
standard `t`-structure of `D_{qc,Z}(X)` lies in Neeman's preferred equivalence class (Neeman,
*Bounded t-structures on the category of perfect complexes*, Acta Math. 233 (2024),
Definitions 2.9–2.10 and Theorem 3.2(iii)).

## What is proved

* `tStructureEquivalent_of_statement` (every `Z`): **if** every object `F` of `D_{qc,Z}(X)`
  such that `Hom(P[-i], F) = 0` for `i ≪ 0` for every compact `P` of `D_{qc,Z}(X)` is bounded
  below (`SupportedDetectsBelowStatement X Z`, the supported form of Stacks 0GFI), then the
  standard `t`-structure `stdT X Z` is equivalent (Neeman's Definition 2.9) to every
  `t`-structure `tG` with `tG^{≥ 1} = {Y | Hom(G[n], Y) = 0 for n ≥ 0}`, for every compact
  generator `G` of `D_{qc,Z}(X)`.
* `supportedDetectsBelowStatement_univ`: the statement holds for `Z = |X|`, from AxiomMath's
  Stacks 0GFI (`Tag0GFIInput`).
* `lemma_A_9_preferred_univ`: **GL26 Lemma A.9, preferred-class clause, for `Z = |X|`**:
  the standard `t`-structure of `D_qc(X)` (as `D_{qc,|X|}(X)`) is equivalent to the
  `t`-structure generated by any compact generator.

## The argument (Neeman's, made uniform by a direct sum)

1. *Uniform bound.*  For a compact generator `G`, an object `F` with `Hom(G[n], F) = 0` for all
   `n ≥ 0` satisfies `Hom(P[-i], F) = 0` for `i ≪ 0` for every compact `P`: `P` lies in the
   triangulated envelope of `G` (Stacks 0GFD with 0AED), and the vanishing range propagates
   through cones (`NeemanAbstract.triangEnvelope_le_bndFrom`).  So, by the supported Stacks 0GFI,
   `F` is bounded below; the direct-sum argument
   (`NeemanAbstract.detectsBelowUniformly_of_detectsBelow`, with the direct sums of Stacks 08F3)
   makes the bound uniform: `tG^{≥ 1} ⊆ D^{≥ -A}`.
2. *The equivalence.*  `G` is perfect (Stacks 0AED), hence bounded above (`G ∈ D^{≤ b}`), and
   `NeemanAbstract.tStructureEquivalent_of_detectsBelowUniformly` gives
   `D^{≤ -N} ⊆ tG^{≤ 0} ⊆ D^{≤ N}` with `N = max(1 - A, b, 1)`.

## What is open (the supported case)

`SupportedDetectsBelowStatement X Z` for a general closed `Z` is the supported form of
Stacks 0GFI ((7) ⇒ (1) inside `D_{qc,Z}(X)`).  AxiomMath proves 0GFI only for `D_QCoh(𝒪_X)`
(`exists_isGE_of_lowHomVanishingOnCompact`), by the induction principle of Stacks 08GP over
elementary distinguished squares with a Koszul complex on the affine member.  A supported version
follows the same induction (Koszul complex on equations of `Z ∩ V` together with those of the
complement of `U ×_W V`, Stacks 09IV for the open member), but its definitions (elementary
distinguished squares, extension by zero, the induction principle) are outside
`scripts/axiommath/spaces-imports.txt`, so it cannot be written in `Spaces` without enlarging that
list.  Neither the statement nor any consequence of it is assumed: it appears only as the
hypothesis of the reduction `tStructureEquivalent_of_statement`.

## Differences from the paper

* "Preferred equivalence class" is rendered as equivalence with *every* `t`-structure `tG`
  whose coaisle is `{Y | Hom(G[n], Y) = 0, n ≥ 0}`, for *every* compact generator `G`.  For the
  `t`-structure compactly generated by `G` (`tG^{≤ 0} = Coprod(G[n], n ≥ 0)`) the coaisle is that
  class (`CompactTStructureW6.ge_one_iff_of_compactlyGenerated`), so this is Neeman's
  Definition 2.10 together with the independence of the generator (Remark 2.11).  The existence
  of `tG` in `D_{qc,Z}(X)` (Alonso–Jeremías–Souto) is not part of the statement: the tree's
  construction `CompactTStructureW6.compactTStructure` sums over the Hom universe `u + 1`,
  while AxiomMath's `D(𝒪_X)` has direct sums indexed by `Type u` only (wave 8,
  `wave8/universe-bridge`).
* Compactness is `IsCompactObject.{u}` (Stacks 07LS, sums indexed by `Type u`), generation is
  `IsPaperGenerator` (zero detection by shifts), the standard `t`-structure is `stdT`
  (`Spaces/Supported/StandardTStructure.lean`).

## Assumptions

Tagged AxiomMath inputs only (`Spaces/Supported/Inputs.lean`): 08F3 and the direct-sum remark
preceding 0AED (direct sums), 0AED and 0GFD (compact objects, classical generation), 0GFI
(`Tag0GFIInput`, for `Z = |X|`) and the boundedness of perfect objects
(`PerfectBoundedAboveInput`).  Neeman 2024, Theorem 3.2 is not assumed.
-/

noncomputable section

open CategoryTheory CategoryTheory.Limits CategoryTheory.Pretriangulated
open CategoryTheory.Triangulated
open AlgebraicGeometry AlgebraicGeometry.Space RelativeWeakApprox

namespace RelativeFM.Spaces.Supported

universe u

attribute [-instance] Stacks.Cohomology.SiteModules.moduleSheavesAbelian
  Stacks.Cohomology.SiteModules.moduleSheavesGrothendieck

attribute [local instance] HasDerivedCategory.standard smallEtaleRingedSite_hasSheafify
  smallEtaleRingedSite_wEqualsLocallyBijective

attribute [local instance] pointTopology

variable {B : BigFppfSite.{u}} {S : Scheme.{u}} {hS : B.Contains S}

/-- **The supported form of Stacks 0GFI** ((7) ⇒ (1)) on `D_{qc,T}(X)`: an object `F` of
`D_{qc,T}(X)` such that, for every compact object `P` of `D_{qc,T}(X)`, `Hom(P[-i], F) = 0` for
all `i ≪ 0`, is bounded below for the standard `t`-structure.  AxiomMath proves it for
`D_QCoh(𝒪_X)` only (`supportedDetectsBelowStatement_univ`); for a general `T` it is **open**
(module docstring) and is not assumed anywhere. -/
def SupportedDetectsBelowStatement (X : AlgebraicSpaces B S hS) [(qcohDerived X).IsTriangulated]
    (T : Set (points B S hS X.1))
    [ObjectProperty.IsTriangulated (CohomologySupportedOn B S hS X.1 X.2 T)] : Prop :=
  ∀ F : DqcZ X T, (∀ P : DqcZ X T, IsCompactObject.{u} P →
      ∃ N : ℤ, ∀ i : ℤ, i ≤ N → ∀ f : P⟦-i⟧ ⟶ F, f = 0) →
    ∃ a : ℤ, (stdT X T).IsGE F a

/-- **The uniform bound** (step 1 of the module docstring): under the supported Stacks 0GFI, a
compact generator `G` of `D_{qc,T}(X)` detects boundedness below uniformly: there is `A` with
`F ∈ D^{≥ A}` whenever `Hom(G[n], F) = 0` for all `n ≥ 0`. -/
theorem detectsBelowUniformly_of_statement (h08F3 : Tag08F3Input B S hS)
    (hsum : SupportedDirectSumsInput B S hS) (h0AED : Tag0AEDInput B S hS)
    (h0GFD : Tag0GFDInput B S hS)
    (X : AlgebraicSpaces B S hS) [(qcohDerived X).IsTriangulated]
    (hXqc : IsQuasiCompactSpace B S hS X.1) (hZ : B.Contains (⊤_ Scheme.{u}))
    (hXqs : IsAbsolutelyQuasiSeparated B S hS hZ X.1)
    (T : Set (points B S hS X.1))
    [ObjectProperty.IsTriangulated (CohomologySupportedOn B S hS X.1 X.2 T)]
    (hT : IsClosed T) (hTc : _root_.IsCompact Tᶜ)
    (hstmt : SupportedDetectsBelowStatement X T)
    (G : DqcZ X T) (hGc : IsCompactObject.{u} G) (hGg : IsPaperGenerator G) :
    DetectsBelowUniformly (stdT X T) G := by
  have := hasCoproducts h08F3 hsum X T hT
  have hGp := (lemma_A_9_isCompactObject_iff h0AED X hXqc hZ hXqs T hT hTc G).1 hGc
  have henv := lemma_A_9_triangEnvelope h0AED h0GFD X hXqc hZ hXqs T hT hTc G hGp hGg
  refine detectsBelowUniformly_of_detectsBelow (stdT X T) hGc fun F hF => hstmt F fun P hP => ?_
  have hPenv : (ObjectProperty.singleton G).triangEnvelope P := by rw [henv]; exact hP
  obtain ⟨m, hm⟩ := triangEnvelope_le_bndFrom G P hPenv
  exact ⟨-m, fun i hi f => hm F hF (-i) (by omega) f⟩

/-- **GL26 Lemma A.9** (`lem:preferred_eq_class`), preferred-class clause, **reduced to the
supported Stacks 0GFI**.  Let `X` be quasi-compact and quasi-separated, `T ⊆ |X|` closed with
quasi-compact complement, and assume `SupportedDetectsBelowStatement X T` (open for general `T`;
proved for `T = |X|` in `supportedDetectsBelowStatement_univ`).  Then for every compact generator
`G` of `D_{qc,T}(X)` and every `t`-structure `tG` with `tG^{≥ 1} = {Y | Hom(G[n], Y) = 0, n ≥ 0}`,
the standard `t`-structure of `D_{qc,T}(X)` is equivalent to `tG` (Neeman 2024, Definition 2.9).
This is a reduction, not the paper's result: its hypothesis `hstmt` is not proved for general
`T`. -/
theorem tStructureEquivalent_of_statement (h08F3 : Tag08F3Input B S hS)
    (hsum : SupportedDirectSumsInput B S hS) (h0AED : Tag0AEDInput B S hS)
    (h0GFD : Tag0GFDInput B S hS) (hbdd : PerfectBoundedAboveInput B S hS)
    (X : AlgebraicSpaces B S hS) [(qcohDerived X).IsTriangulated]
    (hXqc : IsQuasiCompactSpace B S hS X.1) (hZ : B.Contains (⊤_ Scheme.{u}))
    (hXqs : IsAbsolutelyQuasiSeparated B S hS hZ X.1)
    (T : Set (points B S hS X.1))
    [ObjectProperty.IsTriangulated (CohomologySupportedOn B S hS X.1 X.2 T)]
    (hT : IsClosed T) (hTc : _root_.IsCompact Tᶜ)
    (hstmt : SupportedDetectsBelowStatement X T)
    (G : DqcZ X T) (hGc : IsCompactObject.{u} G) (hGg : IsPaperGenerator G)
    (tG : TStructure (DqcZ X T)) (htG : ∀ Y : DqcZ X T, tG.ge 1 Y ↔ genCoaisle G Y) :
    NeemanPreferredM6.TStructureEquivalent (stdT X T) tG := by
  have hGp := (lemma_A_9_isCompactObject_iff h0AED X hXqc hZ hXqs T hT hTc G).1 hGc
  obtain ⟨b, hb⟩ := hbdd hXqc _ hGp
  exact tStructureEquivalent_of_detectsBelowUniformly (stdT X T) tG G b
    ((stdT_isLE_iff X T G b).2 hb) htG
    (detectsBelowUniformly_of_statement h08F3 hsum h0AED h0GFD X hXqc hZ hXqs T hT hTc hstmt G
      hGc hGg)

/-- The inclusion `D_{qc,|X|}(X) ⥤ D_qc(X)` is an equivalence: every object is supported on
`|X|`. -/
instance isEquivalence_ι_univ (X : AlgebraicSpaces B S hS) :
    (qcSupportedOn X (Set.univ : Set (points B S hS X.1))).ι.IsEquivalence where
  essSurj := ⟨fun E => ⟨⟨E, fun _ => Set.subset_univ _⟩, ⟨Iso.refl _⟩⟩⟩

/-- **The supported Stacks 0GFI for `T = |X|`**, from AxiomMath's Stacks 0GFI on
`D_QCoh(𝒪_X)` (`Tag0GFIInput`): compact objects of `D_qc(X)` are compact objects of
`D_{qc,|X|}(X)` along the equivalence `isEquivalence_ι_univ`. -/
theorem supportedDetectsBelowStatement_univ (h0GFI : Tag0GFIInput B S hS)
    (X : AlgebraicSpaces B S hS) [(qcohDerived X).IsTriangulated]
    (hXqc : IsQuasiCompactSpace B S hS X.1) (hZ : B.Contains (⊤_ Scheme.{u}))
    (hXqs : IsAbsolutelyQuasiSeparated B S hS hZ X.1)
    [ObjectProperty.IsTriangulated (CohomologySupportedOn B S hS X.1 X.2 Set.univ)] :
    SupportedDetectsBelowStatement X Set.univ := by
  intro F hF
  let ι := ιZ X Set.univ
  have hι := fullyFaithfulιZ X Set.univ
  obtain ⟨a, ha⟩ := h0GFI hZ X hXqc hXqs F.obj fun P hP => by
    let P' : DqcZ X Set.univ := ⟨P, fun _ => Set.subset_univ _⟩
    have hP' : IsCompactObject.{u} P' :=
      (isCompactObject_iff_isCompactObject_obj (qcSupportedOn X Set.univ).ι P').2 hP
    obtain ⟨N, hN⟩ := hF P' hP'
    refine ⟨N, fun i hi => ⟨fun x y => ?_⟩⟩
    have key : ∀ z : P.obj⟦-i⟧ ⟶ F.obj.obj, z = 0 := fun z => by
      have h0 := hN i hi (hι.preimage ((ι.commShiftIso (-i)).hom.app P' ≫ z))
      have h1 := congrArg ι.map h0
      rw [hι.map_preimage, Functor.map_zero] at h1
      rw [← cancel_epi ((ι.commShiftIso (-i)).hom.app P'), h1, comp_zero]
    rw [key x, key y]
  exact ⟨a, (stdT_isGE_iff X Set.univ F a).2 ha⟩

/-- **GL26 Lemma A.9** (`lem:preferred_eq_class`), **preferred-class clause for `Z = |X|`**:
for a quasi-compact quasi-separated algebraic space `X`, the standard `t`-structure of
`D_qc(X)` (as `D_{qc,|X|}(X)`) is equivalent (Neeman 2024, Definition 2.9) to every
`t`-structure `tG` with `tG^{≥ 1} = {Y | Hom(G[n], Y) = 0, n ≥ 0}`, for every compact generator
`G` (a compact generator exists: `lemma_A_9_generator`).  From AxiomMath's Stacks 08F3, 0AED,
0GFD, 0GFI and the boundedness of perfect objects; Neeman's theorem is not assumed.
**Difference from the paper**: `Z = |X|` only (the supported case is reduced to the open
`SupportedDetectsBelowStatement` in `tStructureEquivalent_of_statement`), and the existence of
the compactly generated `tG` is not part of the statement (module docstring). -/
theorem lemma_A_9_preferred_univ (h08F3 : Tag08F3Input B S hS)
    (hsum : SupportedDirectSumsInput B S hS) (h0AED : Tag0AEDInput B S hS)
    (h0GFD : Tag0GFDInput B S hS) (h0GFI : Tag0GFIInput B S hS)
    (hbdd : PerfectBoundedAboveInput B S hS)
    (X : AlgebraicSpaces B S hS) [(qcohDerived X).IsTriangulated]
    (hXqc : IsQuasiCompactSpace B S hS X.1) (hZ : B.Contains (⊤_ Scheme.{u}))
    (hXqs : IsAbsolutelyQuasiSeparated B S hS hZ X.1)
    [ObjectProperty.IsTriangulated (CohomologySupportedOn B S hS X.1 X.2 Set.univ)]
    (G : DqcZ X Set.univ) (hGc : IsCompactObject.{u} G) (hGg : IsPaperGenerator G)
    (tG : TStructure (DqcZ X Set.univ))
    (htG : ∀ Y : DqcZ X Set.univ, tG.ge 1 Y ↔ genCoaisle G Y) :
    NeemanPreferredM6.TStructureEquivalent (stdT X Set.univ) tG :=
  tStructureEquivalent_of_statement h08F3 hsum h0AED h0GFD hbdd X hXqc hZ hXqs Set.univ
    isClosed_univ (by rw [Set.compl_univ]; exact isCompact_empty)
    (supportedDetectsBelowStatement_univ h0GFI X hXqc hZ hXqs) G hGc hGg tG htG

/-- **GL26 Lemma A.9, preferred-class clause for `Z = |X|`, uniform bound**: a compact
generator `G` of `D_qc(X)` detects boundedness below uniformly — there is `A` with
`F ∈ D^{≥ A}` for every `F` with `Hom(G[n], F) = 0` for all `n ≥ 0`.  This is the
universe-independent content of the preferred-class clause (the coaisle inclusion
`tG^{≥ 1} ⊆ D^{≥ A}`), with no `t`-structure `tG` in the statement. -/
theorem lemma_A_9_detectsBelowUniformly_univ (h08F3 : Tag08F3Input B S hS)
    (hsum : SupportedDirectSumsInput B S hS) (h0AED : Tag0AEDInput B S hS)
    (h0GFD : Tag0GFDInput B S hS) (h0GFI : Tag0GFIInput B S hS)
    (X : AlgebraicSpaces B S hS) [(qcohDerived X).IsTriangulated]
    (hXqc : IsQuasiCompactSpace B S hS X.1) (hZ : B.Contains (⊤_ Scheme.{u}))
    (hXqs : IsAbsolutelyQuasiSeparated B S hS hZ X.1)
    [ObjectProperty.IsTriangulated (CohomologySupportedOn B S hS X.1 X.2 Set.univ)]
    (G : DqcZ X Set.univ) (hGc : IsCompactObject.{u} G) (hGg : IsPaperGenerator G) :
    DetectsBelowUniformly (stdT X Set.univ) G :=
  detectsBelowUniformly_of_statement h08F3 hsum h0AED h0GFD X hXqc hZ hXqs Set.univ
    isClosed_univ (by rw [Set.compl_univ]; exact isCompact_empty)
    (supportedDetectsBelowStatement_univ h0GFI X hXqc hZ hXqs) G hGc hGg

/-! ### Non-vacuity -/

/-- **Non-vacuity of `lemma_A_9_detectsBelowUniformly_univ`**: at the algebraic space `X = h_{T₀}`
represented by an affine object `T₀` of the site (`hX`, satisfied by `rfl`), every hypothesis is
met (the instance arguments
by `nonVacuity_instances`), a compact generator `G` of `D_qc(X)` exists, and it detects
boundedness below uniformly for the standard `t`-structure. -/
theorem nonVacuity_detectsBelowUniformly_affine
    (h08F3 : Tag08F3Input B S hS) (hsum : SupportedDirectSumsInput B S hS)
    (h0AEC : Tag0AECInput B S hS) (h0AED : Tag0AEDInput B S hS) (h0GFD : Tag0GFDInput B S hS)
    (h0GFI : Tag0GFIInput B S hS)
    (hqs : AffineQuasiSeparatedInput B S hS) (hterm : ContainsTerminalInput.{u})
    (T₀ : BigFppfOver B S hS) (hT₀ : IsAffine ((BigFppfOver.toScheme B S hS).obj T₀))
    (X : AlgebraicSpaces B S hS) (hX : X = representedSpace T₀)
    [(qcohDerived X).IsTriangulated]
    [ObjectProperty.IsTriangulated (CohomologySupportedOn B S hS X.1 X.2 Set.univ)] :
    ∃ G : DqcZ X Set.univ, IsCompactObject.{u} G ∧ IsPaperGenerator G ∧
      DetectsBelowUniformly (stdT X Set.univ) G := by
  obtain ⟨hqc, hqs', hcl, hco⟩ := nonVacuity_affine_univ hqs (hterm B) T₀ hT₀
  rw [← hX] at hqc hqs' hcl hco
  obtain ⟨G, -, hGc, hGg⟩ :=
    lemma_A_9_generator h0AEC h0AED X hqc (hterm B) hqs' Set.univ hcl hco
  exact ⟨G, hGc, hGg, lemma_A_9_detectsBelowUniformly_univ h08F3 hsum h0AED h0GFD h0GFI
    X hqc (hterm B) hqs' G hGc hGg⟩

/-- The two instance arguments of `nonVacuity_detectsBelowUniformly_affine` (and of every
theorem of this file) are satisfied: they are Stacks 06UQ and `SupportTriangulatedInput`. -/
theorem nonVacuity_instances (h06 : Tag06UQInput B S hS) (hsupp : SupportTriangulatedInput B S hS)
    (X : AlgebraicSpaces B S hS) (T : Set (points B S hS X.1)) :
    (qcohDerived X).IsTriangulated ∧
      ObjectProperty.IsTriangulated (CohomologySupportedOn B S hS X.1 X.2 T) :=
  ⟨isTriangulated_qcohDerived h06 X, isTriangulated_support hsupp X T⟩

end RelativeFM.Spaces.Supported
